('giant_ant_worker','Giant Ant, Worker','Giant Ant, Worker','1','Medium','Vermin','','2d8 (9 hp)',9,'+0','50 ft. (10 squares), climb 20 ft.','17 (+7 natural), touch 10, flat-footed 17','+1/+1','Bite +1 melee (1d6)','5 ft./5 ft.','+3','+0','+0',10,10,10,null,11,9,'Climb +8','TrackB','{"special_attacks":"Improved grab","special_qualities":"Scent, vermin traits"}'::jsonb,'Giant ants are among the hardiest and most adaptable vermin. Soldiers and workers are about 6 feet long, while queens can grow to a length of 9 feet.

**Acid Sting (Ex):** A giant soldier ant has a stinger and an acid-producing gland in its abdomen. If it successfully grabs an opponent, it can attempt to sting each round (+3 attack bonus). A hit with the sting attack deals 1d4+1 points of piercing damage and 1d4 points of acid damage.

**Improved Grab (Ex):** To use this ability, a giant ant must hit with its bite attack. A giant soldier ant that wins the ensuing grapple check establishes a hold and can sting.

**Skills:** \*Giant ants have a +4 racial bonus on Survival checks when tracking by scent and a +8 racial bonus on Climb checks. A giant ant can always choose to take 10 on Climb checks, even if rushed or threatened.','{"full_attack":"Bite +1 melee (1d6)","environment":"Temperate plains","organization":"Gang (2–6) or crew (6–11 plus 1 giant ant soldier)","treasure":"None","advancement":"3–4 HD (Medium); 5–6 HD (Large)","level_adjustment":"—","statblock":{"hit_dice":"2d8 (9 hp)","hit_points":9,"base_attack_grapple":"+1/+1","attack":"Bite +1 melee (1d6)","full_attack":"Bite +1 melee (1d6)","space_reach":"5 ft./5 ft.","saves":"Fort +3, Ref +0, Will +0","abilities":{"str":"10","dex":"10","con":"10","int":null,"wis":"11","cha":"9"},"skills":"Climb +8","feats":"TrackB","special_attacks":"Improved grab","special_qualities":"Scent, vermin traits"},"source_file":"monsters-vermin.md","source_dataset":"olimot/srd-v3.5-md"}'::jsonb,'https://olimot.github.io/srd-v3.5/monsters/monsters-vermin.html',true),
('giant_ant_soldier','Giant Ant, Soldier','Giant Ant, Soldier','2','Medium','Vermin','','2d8+2 (11 hp)',11,'+0','50 ft. (10 squares), climb 20 ft.','17 (+7 natural), touch 10, flat-footed 17','+1/+3','Bite +3 melee (2d4+3)','5 ft./5 ft.','+4','+0','+1',14,10,13,null,13,11,'Climb +10','TrackB','{"special_attacks":"Improved grab, acid sting","special_qualities":"Scent, vermin traits"}'::jsonb,'Giant ants are among the hardiest and most adaptable vermin. Soldiers and workers are about 6 feet long, while queens can grow to a length of 9 feet.

**Acid Sting (Ex):** A giant soldier ant has a stinger and an acid-producing gland in its abdomen. If it successfully grabs an opponent, it can attempt to sting each round (+3 attack bonus). A hit with the sting attack deals 1d4+1 points of piercing damage and 1d4 points of acid damage.

**Improved Grab (Ex):** To use this ability, a giant ant must hit with its bite attack. A giant soldier ant that wins the ensuing grapple check establishes a hold and can sting.

